{
  "name": "258. Vertex session routing from prompt_cache_key (session routing)",
  "description": "use_session_routing on a Vertex key sends the request's prompt cache key to Gemini models as session_id. Vertex routes requests with the same session ID to one replica, so stateless requests that share a long prefix and differ in the question read it from the implicit cache (Google enables session routing per project). Each route carries the key in its own field: prompt_cache_key on /v1/chat/completions and /v1/responses (unary and streamed), metadata.user_id on /anthropic, and session_id on /genai (a string, or the Gemini API's int64, sent on as a string). Rows read the Vertex-bound request back from the log. Guards: a Vertex key without the flag sends nothing; the Gemini API, whose session_id is an int64, never receives one (a leaked string would answer 400); /genai countTokens with session_id still answers, since Vertex rejects session_id there. Requests pin the key by name (x-bf-api-key), since two profile keys can serve Gemini models. Red before the feature: rows 1-7 reach Vertex without session_id.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "258.1 vertex/gemini-3.7-flash /v1/chat/completions prompt_cache_key is sent as session_id (session routing)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var reqId = pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-request-id');",
              "pm.test('258.1 vertex/gemini-3.7-flash /v1/chat/completions prompt_cache_key is sent as session_id (session routing) succeeds', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text().slice(0, 500)).to.equal(200);",
              "  pm.expect(reqId, 'x-bifrost-request-id header').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code !== 200 || !reqId) { return; }",
              "// The log row is written by the batching writer, so poll for it. Bounded: ten reads a second apart.",
              "function checkLog(attempt) {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('baseUrl') + '/api/logs/' + reqId, method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "    var rr = null;",
              "    if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
              "      rr = res.json().raw_request;",
              "      if (typeof rr === 'string') { try { rr = JSON.parse(rr); } catch (e) { rr = null; } }",
              "    }",
              "    if (rr) {",
              "      pm.test('the request reached Vertex with session ID harness-session-chat', function () {",
              "        pm.expect(rr.session_id, 'raw_request: ' + JSON.stringify(rr).slice(0, 400)).to.equal('harness-session-chat');",
              "        pm.expect(rr.sessionId, 'camelCase sessionId sent: ' + JSON.stringify(rr).slice(0, 400)).to.equal(undefined);",
              "      });",
              "      return;",
              "    }",
              "    if (attempt < 10) { setTimeout(function () { checkLog(attempt + 1); }, 1000); return; }",
              "    pm.test('log row carries the provider-bound raw_request', function () { pm.expect.fail('log ' + reqId + ' never carried raw_request: ' + (err ? String(err) : (res.code + ' ' + res.text().slice(0, 300)))); });",
              "  });",
              "}",
              "checkLog(0);"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-store-raw-request-response",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "Vertex Global (Gemini 3)"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"vertex/gemini-3.7-flash\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 64,\n  \"prompt_cache_key\": \"harness-session-chat\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Say ok.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
